// PIN DM-02 — `==` between arrays answered #0 only in the register VM.
// Closed 2026-08-18 by adding the `Array` arm to `Value::equals` and
// `cmp_direct` in zymbol-vm/src/lib.rs; both had a `Tuple` arm and no `Array`
// one, so arrays fell through to `_ => false`.
//
// Why the pin is worth its line: `corpus/bugs/bug_vm_tuple_equality.zy` had
// covered the same question FOR TUPLES since v0.0.5, and the neighbouring case
// is exactly what made the gap feel covered. A pin that is one line away from
// an existing case is the kind that gets talked out of existence.
//
// Measuring it turned up a second divergence, fixed at the same time and
// asserted here too: `[1, 2, 3] == [1, 2.0, 3]`. `1 == 1.0` is #1, so element
// equality has to be the same relation as scalar equality.
//
// Named-tuple equality is DM-22 and was deliberately NOT fixed. It is not
// asserted here — a pin that quietly covers an open finding reports it as
// closed.
a = [1, 2, 3]
b = [1, 2, 3]
>> (a == b) ¶
c = [1, 2.0, 3]
>> (a == c) ¶
>> ([] == []) ¶
>> ([[1, 2], [3]] == [[1, 2], [3]]) ¶
>> (a <> [1, 2, 4]) ¶
